DECISIONS 213, 403, CODEGEN.md §7.9: a broken duplicate of b's own const LIMIT, carrying @cpp(defines:), is no define of b, so it does not stand for LIMIT: z, which b does not read, writes the #define LIMIT and b's const LIMIT is E8005 foreignDefine, beside the E2106 of the broken duplicate.
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
  roots {
    out: "out"
  }
}
-- z/z.canon --
/// Z.
package z

/// The limit, a macro and a C++ constant of one name.
@cpp(defines: "")
const LIMIT = 9

emit cpp { out: "@out/z", namespace: "z", mode: types }
-- b/b.canon --
/// B.
package b

/// The limit.
const LIMIT = 7

/// The limit again, a broken duplicate.
@cpp(defines: "")
const LIMIT = 8

emit cpp { out: "@out/b", namespace: "b", mode: types }
-- check-only --
-- select --
b
-- findings.txt --
error[E8005]  b/b.canon:5:7
  LIMIT is declared for b.LIMIT and written as a #define for z.LIMIT, in a package this one does not read, so its headers cannot guard it; rename b.LIMIT with @cpp(name:), or use a type of that package here

error[E2106]  b/b.canon:9:7
  LIMIT is declared twice (first at b/b.canon:5)

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
